# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository *and* in working copies.
#
# Not a style preference: plan provenance hashes source files byte for byte
# (`engine_source_sha256`, `notebook_generator_sha256`, the candidate manifests),
# and the generator tests compare a freshly built notebook against the stored
# one. A CRLF checkout — which `core.autocrlf=true` produces on Windows by
# default — changes those hashes and fails the tests without any file having
# actually changed. `eol=lf` pins the working copy so the hashes hold on every
# platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The repository's own PowerShell hooks follow the platform convention; nothing
# hashes them.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary artefacts (most should never be committed anyway — belt and braces)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.parquet binary
*.onnx binary
*.gguf binary
